    {
      "id": "fp0yzff",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. EXCHANGE RATE DETERMINATION (DEMAND–SUPPLY THEORY)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Exchange rates are primarily determined by the market forces of demand and supply in the foreign exchange market.",
        "Rupee depreciation makes exports cheaper for foreign buyers and imports more expensive for domestic consumers.",
        "Rupee appreciation makes imports cheaper while making domestic exports less cost-competitive abroad.",
        "Analyzing India's major trade partners and export-import composition is essential for understanding the country's balance of trade.",
        "RRB high-value exam questions frequently test the economic effects of currency value fluctuations on trade deficits."
      ],
      "id": "5aoe7h1"
    },
